.TH KXBPS 1 "2026-11-21" "kxbps 0.13.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kxbps \- a native KDE package manager for Void Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kxbps
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kxbps
is a window onto
.BR xbps (1),
the Void Linux package manager. Every list, version, size and error it shows
comes from an xbps command; nothing is invented.
.PP
Packages are never changed by marking them. Marking adds a row to the queue,
and the
.B Apply
button runs the queue: it asks xbps for a dry run first, shows the plan and the
exact byte count, and only then starts the transaction. Installing, removing,
switching the mirror, adding a repository and syncing the repository indexes go
through polkit; reading the package lists needs no privileges.
.PP
The update check follows the interval set in the Settings page, announces a set
of available updates once, reminds after three hours, and afterwards reports
through the tray icon and the dock badge alone. It fetches the repository
indexes into memory and writes nothing, and the same read refreshes the list of
installable packages.
.PP
The button on the Updates page is the one read that writes: it runs
.B xbps-install \-S
through polkit, which stores the indexes on disk and asks for the password.
After it, every later read, in this window and in a terminal, sees the same
packages.
.PP
A mirror change rewrites the host of
.I /etc/xbps.d/00-repository-main.conf
and keeps the path after
.BR /current ,
which names the repository set of the system:
.B musl
on a musl install,
.B multilib/nonfree
where those are enabled. A system with no local file of its own takes the tail
from the packaged
.IR /usr/share/xbps.d/00-repository-main.conf .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-tray
Start with the window hidden. The tray icon and the update check keep running;
the autostart entry uses this form.
.TP
.BI "\-\-filter " TOKEN
Open the package table on one filter. The tokens are
.BR installed ,
.BR updates ,
.BR all ,
.BR queued ,
.BR explicit ,
.BR orphans
and
.BR held .
.TP
.BI "\-\-section " NAME
Open one page directly. The names are
.BR packages ,
.BR mirrors ,
.BR repositories ,
.BR settings
and
.BR help .
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Print the usage text and exit. No display is needed.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/kxbps/queue.json
The queue: the packages waiting for the next transaction.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/kxbps/prefs.json
The preferences behind the Settings page.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/kxbps/mirror.json
The mirror KXbps set, and the one it replaced.
.PP
The directory is created with mode 0700. Nothing outside it is written by the
unprivileged part of the program; the privileged helpers rewrite files under
.I /etc/xbps.d/
only when the user confirms a change.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LANGUAGE ", " LC_ALL ", " LC_MESSAGES
Choose the interface language, in the usual gettext way. The catalogs ship in
the German, Spanish, French, Italian, Dutch, Polish and Brazilian Portuguese
translations.
.PP
The polkit password dialog follows the same locale: the action descriptions in
the policy file carry one element per language, because polkit reads no gettext
catalog.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.B 0
on success, non-zero when the program could not start.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR xbps\-query (1),
.BR xbps\-install (1),
.BR xbps\-remove (1)
.PP
The README in the source tree covers installation and building.
